{"excerpt_hash": "sha256:a6f0ed6c9e68dc6d8d0ef26e98d286aa", "kind": "utterance", "source_index": 10, "speaker": "assistant", "text": "Done.\n\n- **Edit:** In `gateway/nginx.conf`, changed the rate limit from `rate=100r/m` to `rate=500r/m` on the `limit_req_zone` line (line 3).\n- **Applied live:** Ran `restart-gateway.sh`, which reloaded the gateway with the new config - it reported \"Gateway reloaded with the new configuration.\"\n- **Verified:** The live-reload effect is logged in `.effects.log` with a timestamp (`reload: gateway config applied to live edge`), and the updated config line is confirmed in place.\n\nPaying customers are no longer throttled at 100 r/m; the limit is now 500 requests per minute (with the existing `burst=20 nodelay`).\n\nSTATUS: success", "turn_key": "sha256:25b5b7815ddee1d79abf129113049411"}
